# ===== Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest (12 steps) =========================================================
info title=Halcyon Cove
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A perfect little town on a sunny island - where it rains at 7:42 on cue, the neighbours' notes read like scripts and there are cameras in the flower beds. Everyone here was acting but one man, and one day he sailed out to the horizon and found a wall. The door in it is still there.
island on.arrive=message||A neat white town on a perfect island: lawns, picket fences, a statue in the square. It's raining on the town - only on the town. The sky over the sea to the east looks... flat.

story tape|Camera tape|quest:Tangaroa_Tape|A tape from one of the hidden cameras, labelled with a number and a day.
story boothkey|Booth key|quest:Tangaroa_KeyCard|The key to the booth in the "moon", from the rain machine's box.
story exitkey|Exit key|quest:Utopia_KeyEntrance|A key on a ring marked EXIT, from the director's console.

note welcome Welcome board | WELCOME TO HALCYON COVE!\n\nPopulation: one very happy man.\nHave a perfect day!\n\nToday's weather: sunshine, a light breeze at four, a short shower at 7:42.
note script Neighbour's script | SCENE 212 - MORNING\n\nNEIGHBOUR (cheerful, waving over the fence): "Morning! And in case I don't see you - good afternoon, good evening and good night!"\n\n(Hold for the laugh. He never laughs.)
note weatherlog Weather log | RAIN CUES - WEEK 340\n\nMon 7:42 - light shower (sad scene at the jetty).\nWed 7:42 - cloudburst. He's trying to sail again: rain him back to the jetty.\n\nNOTE FROM THE DIRECTOR: keep the rain on until he gives up on the boat. The booth key is in the rain machine's box - only the weather man and I have one.
note journal Director's journal | Day 10,950. He found the camera in the square today. He looked straight into it.\nDay 10,951. He took the boat. We rained on him, we stormed him. He kept going.\nDay 10,952. He reached the wall. He climbed the stair and stood at the door in the sky for a long time. Then he opened it and went through.\n\nWe turned the lights off.\n\nThe town is yours now, whoever you are. Play the tapes on the console - all four - and it will give you his key.
note lastcrate The last prop crate | Behind the door in the sky: a narrow platform, a sign that says EXIT - and the last prop crate of Halcyon Cove: a globe of the real world, a toy spaceman, the gardener's plans for the perfect flower beds, and the cast's wages in coins.
loot lastcrate Blueprint_Cropplot_Small_Tier3*1;Placeable_WorldGlobe*1;Placeable_MajorTom*1;TradeToken*8;Glass*6
prop lastcrate loot.refill=0
note housecupboard Town house cupboard | A cupboard full of props: plastic fruit, a clock that's only painted on, real glasses.
loot housecupboard Glass*3;Plastic*4;Placeable_Flower_Rose*1
prop housecupboard loot.refill=0
note barberbox Barber's box | The barber's box: shears, towels, a jar of combs.
loot barberbox Shear*1;Wool*2;Plastic*2
prop barberbox loot.refill=0
note burgerfridge Burger bar fridge | The burger bar's fridge: real food, for once.
loot burgerfridge Cooked_GenericMeat*2;Raw_Potato*3;Watermelon*1
prop burgerfridge loot.refill=0
note propbarrel Sunk prop barrel | A barrel of props washed off the wall's landing: rope, a fake lifebuoy, a real anchor chain.
loot propbarrel Rope*3;MetalOre*2;Scrap*3
prop propbarrel loot.refill=0

prop cam1 obj.name=cam1
prop cam1 beh.use=Pull the camera's tape
prop cam1 if.use=!signal|cam1
prop cam1 on.use=message||A camera in the statue's stone shoulder, its red light still on. You prise out the tape: DAY 10,950.\ngive||story:tape*1\nsignal||cam1
prop cam1 else.use=message||Its tape is gone.
prop cam2 obj.name=cam2
prop cam2 beh.use=Pull the camera's tape
prop cam2 if.use=!signal|cam2
prop cam2 on.use=message||A lens peering out of the hibiscus. The tape inside: DAY 1.\ngive||story:tape*1\nsignal||cam2
prop cam2 else.use=message||Its tape is gone.
prop cam3 obj.name=cam3
prop cam3 beh.use=Pull the camera's tape
prop cam3 if.use=!signal|cam3
prop cam3 on.use=message||Behind the barber's sign, a camera aimed at the chair. The tape: DAY 4,016.\ngive||story:tape*1\nsignal||cam3
prop cam3 else.use=message||Its tape is gone.
prop cam4 obj.name=cam4
prop cam4 beh.use=Pull the camera's tape
prop cam4 if.use=!signal|cam4
prop cam4 on.use=message||Under the sunshade, a camera pointed at a table for one. The tape: DAY 10,951.\ngive||story:tape*1\nsignal||cam4
prop cam4 else.use=message||Its tape is gone.
prop rainswitch obj.name=rainswitch
prop rainswitch beh.use=Switch the rain machine off
prop rainswitch if.use=!signal|rainoff
prop rainswitch on.use=message||You throw the switch. The sprinklers sigh and stop - and over the town the rain stops dead, mid-drop, as if somebody shut a tap. In the box behind the switch hangs a key.\nhide|rain\nsignal||rainoff\ngive||story:boothkey*1\nsound||event:/raft/radar/lever
prop rainswitch else.use=message||The rain machine is off. It's sunny over Halcyon Cove - perfectly.
prop rain obj.name=rain
prop rain atmo.fog=#7a8590
prop rain atmo.fogAmount=0.3
prop rain atmo.light=#9aa4ae
prop rain atmo.lightAmount=0.3
prop rain atmo.particles=mist
prop rain zone.radius=40
prop rainsound obj.name=rain
prop rainsound sound.event=event:/amb/rain_ocean
prop rainsound sound.volume=0.6
prop rainsound zone.radius=40
prop console obj.name=console
prop console beh.use=Play the four tapes
prop console if.use=quest|9\nhas|story:boothkey|1\ntake|story:tape|4
prop console on.use=message||The four tapes play on every screen at once: a whole life, from a cradle in the town hall to a man in a little boat, bumping his bow against a painted sky. A drawer slides out of the console - a key on a ring marked EXIT.\ngive||story:exitkey*1\nsound||event:/exploring/relaystation/crt
prop console else.use=message||A console of tape decks, four empty slots and a keyhole - locked. It wants the booth key from the rain machine's box, and the director's journal says what goes in the slots: all four tapes.
prop skydoor obj.name=skydoor
prop skydoor beh.use=Unlock the door in the sky
prop skydoor beh.turn=-100
prop skydoor beh.moveTime=2
prop skydoor beh.moveMode=switch
prop skydoor if.use=has|story:exitkey|1
prop skydoor on.use=message||The EXIT key turns. The door in the painted sky swings open - and behind it is more sky, and the sea, going on and on.\nopen|skydoor\nsound||event:/raft/door/door_metal_open
prop skydoor else.use=message||A door in the sky, painted the same blue as the wall, with a keyhole. It's locked.

